From 982e0c3b2b681d113beb7531aea287cf96e41839 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: max rossi <113717219+maxr0ssi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:07:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] wined3d: Record linked GLSL programs and build them
 again in idle CS time in later runs.

Linking a GL program takes 3-7 ms on macOS, and wined3d links each program the first time a
draw needs it, so every new combination of shaders and state is a hitch; a game meeting a new
unit or effect links a dozen at once. Record what each program was linked from - the byte code
hash and compile arguments of its D3D shaders, or its fixed function settings, and the state the
link itself depends on - in %LOCALAPPDATA%\wined3d\<executable>.glslprograms. In later runs, queue
each recorded program once the D3D shaders it needs have been created (fixed function ones at
once), pairing a shader with the most recently created shader for the other stage, and build the
queue while the CS thread has nothing else to do, one program at a time. A program built ahead
is only found by the ordinary lookup at draw time, which compares GL shader objects, so it is only
used where the draw would have linked exactly the same program. The file starts over when the
record layout changes. WINED3D_PROGRAM_CACHE=0 disables recording and building.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
