+/* GLSL program cache.
+ *
+ * Linking a GL program takes milliseconds with some drivers (3-7 ms on macOS), and wined3d links
+ * each program when a draw first needs it, so every new combination of shaders and state is a
+ * hitch in the frame that meets it. Record what each linked program was built from - the byte code
+ * hashes and compile arguments of its D3D shaders, or the fixed function settings - in a file
+ * under the user's local application data, one per executable. In later runs, build those
+ * programs again while the CS thread has nothing else to do, as soon as the D3D shaders they need
+ * exist. A program built ahead is only found by the ordinary lookup at draw time, which compares
+ * GL shader objects, i.e. only where the draw would have built exactly the same program.
+ * WINED3D_PROGRAM_CACHE=0 disables recording and building. */
